Hi! 

Maddie from Originality.AI here...

I was curious if you've had a chance to check out our**Accuracy Case
Study** <https://jonhaver.lt.acemlnb.com/Prod/link-tracker?redirectUrl=aHR0cHMlM0ElMkYlMkZvcmlnaW5hbGl0eS5haSUyRmJsb2clMkZhaS1jb250ZW50LWRldGVjdGlvbi1hY2N1cmFjeQ==&sig=DQnewfiuo3dQCdri3unK1V8FNBc4jgF7SLCuoAUH5YMp&iat=1691766483&a=%7C%7C798597961%7C%7C&account=jonhaver%2Eactivehosted%2Ecom&email=JJWqwUwcducRXAlzdUWM%2F72IjGzV2LgQA%2BVJ5KeKe7mYd4orIrTp3i9IGWU%3D%3AdTIxK7BfDt3PguYMUQbx5U8NBRJnTI3H&s=c2aa77b6f0a29bb9a1c1a13f88329783&i=1934A2098A61A29782> that
we published last week? 

The reason we felt so strongly about publishing something like this was
because we wanted to set a standard of transparency and accountability
within our industry. 

Unfortunately unsubstantiated AI detector claims have resulted in
a lot of skepticism and mistrust.

Our hope is that digging deep into the data, and open sourcing tools to
help others do so too, helps to bridge the gap. 

**How we view AI Generated Content...**

1. We are not Anti-AI! In fact, 

**we love AI** and think that it absolutely has its place! We just
strongly believe that the person who has purchased the content should
know whether it is AI Generated or not in order to be able to make an
informed decision as to the risks associated with publishing AI
generated content. 

2. We believe that AI Content Detection plays an important role in
mitigating some of the societal risks that AI Generated content can lead
to ( Mass propaganda, fake news, cheating etc).

3. We believe that with this important role, AI Detection Companies have
the responsibility to communicate the accuracy and limitations of their
tools transparently.

4. We believe that this transparent communication will help push
companies to be better and more accountable when they are developing
their AI systems.

What Happens if AI Generated Content is Undetectable?

**Recent example of the potential negative impact... NY Times Article
Featuring Originality.ai Identifying AI Generated & Wrong Travel
Guidebooks: **

A NY Times investigation using Originality identified Travel Guide Books
being published & sold on Amazon that were AI generated (which had
factual errors).

